#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/2
msgid ""
"We're no longer constantly on the run from la\n"
"Guardia or mercenaries.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不再需要时刻躲避国民警卫队\n"
"或雇佣兵了。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/3
msgid ""
"Some of the new guys we've recruited used to be\n"
"mercenaries...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们招募的一些新人以前就是\n"
"雇佣兵……\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/4
msgid ""
"We're getting along. It was difficult at first,\n"
msgstr ""
"我们处得来。一开始挺难的，\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/5
msgid ""
"but once you talk to them you realize we've got\n"
"plenty in common.\n"
msgstr ""
"但一交谈，就会发现我们\n"
"有很多共同点。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/6
msgid ""
"I see. Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，那就好。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/7
msgid ""
"We may be enemies, but we're all still human\n"
"beings...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们也许是敌人，但终究都是\n"
"人类……\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/8
msgid ""
"La CIA's soldiers, la Guardia... The same goes for\n"
"the people of America.\n"
msgstr ""
"中情局士兵、国民警卫队……\n"
"美国人民也一样。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/9
msgid ""
"What's gotten into you?\n"
msgstr ""
"你怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/10
msgid ""
"Mi viejo got involved with drugs in order to scrape\n"
"together money for la revolución.\n"
msgstr ""
"我老爸为了给革命凑钱，\n"
"卷入了毒品交易。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/11
msgid ""
"He did whatever the KGB said.\n"
msgstr ""
"克格勃让他干什么他就干什么。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/12
msgid ""
"All for Nicaragua... or so he told himself.\n"
msgstr ""
"全为尼加拉瓜，他这么想。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/13
msgid ""
"But I realize now... In the end all he did was help\n"
"poison young people of America.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我现在明白……到头来他只是帮\n"
"毒害美国年轻人。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/15
msgid ""
"...I've made up my mind. Even when I leave Mother\n"
"Base and return to la revolución,\n"
msgstr ""
"……我已经下定决心。即使我离开母基地\n"
"回到革命中，\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/16
msgid ""
"I will never turn to drugs. Nor will I look to the KGB\n"
"for help.\n"
msgstr ""
"我绝不碰毒品。也不向克格勃\n"
"求助。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/17
msgid ""
"If we topple Somoza using the KGB and drug\n"
"money, we will lose the people's hearts.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果我们用克格勃和毒品资金\n"
"推翻索摩查，我们将失去民心。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/18
msgid ""
"So you're choosing a different path from your\n"
"father.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你选了条与你父亲\n"
"不同的路。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/19
msgid ""
"I still respect him. But I will not do things the way\n"
"he did.\n"
msgstr ""
"我仍尊敬他。但不会照\n"
"他的方式行事。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/20
msgid ""
"Well, I'm sure Chico will be glad to hear that.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科听到肯定高兴。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/21
msgid ""
"Chico is a grown soldier now. I could not face him\n"
"otherwise.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科现在是真正战士了。\n"
"不然我没脸见他。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/22
msgid ""
"Well said, Amanda. Those are the words of a true\n"
"comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"说得好，阿曼达。这是\n"
"真正指挥官的话。\n"

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/23
msgid ""
"Stop... I was inspired by the greatest comandante I\n"
"have ever known, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"别……我是受我所见过\n"
"最伟大的指挥官BOSS鼓舞。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, how do I get to the prison camp?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，怎么去战俘营？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/1
msgid ""
"First head up the narrow mountain path.\n"
msgstr ""
"先沿狭窄的山路上行。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/2
msgid ""
"The path will gradually open up, and you'll come to\n"
"a fork in the road.\n"
msgstr ""
"道路会逐渐开阔，你会来到\n"
"一个岔路口。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/3
msgid ""
"Watch yourself up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"上面小心点。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/4
msgid ""
"You'll be lower than the surrounding terrain,\n"
msgstr ""
"你会处于周围地形之下，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/5
msgid ""
"so if you head down the middle you'll make for an\n"
"easy target.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以走中间，就会成为\n"
"容易的目标。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/6
msgid ""
"Thanks for the heads-up.\n"
msgstr ""
"多谢提醒。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/7
msgid ""
"Take the leftward path to reach the prison camp.\n"
msgstr ""
"走左边的路就能到战俘营。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 431..1030
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/0
msgid ""
"What can you tell me about the prison camp?\n"
msgstr ""
"战俘营的情况怎么样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 1058..2117
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/1
msgid ""
"Well, it used to be a village - until they took control\n"
"of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，这里曾是村庄，直到他们\n"
"控制了它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 2145..3065
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/2
msgid ""
"It is a maze of paths, so watch out for soldiers on\n"
"patrol.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里道路交错，要小心\n"
"巡逻的士兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 3301..3956
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/3
msgid ""
"I'll be sure not to stop and say \"hi.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我肯定不会停下来打招呼。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 3984..4931
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/4
msgid ""
"Use the paths carefully and you should be able to\n"
"stay out of view.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心利用这些道路，你应该能够\n"
"避开视线。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 4959..5489
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/5
msgid ""
"Where are they holding Chico?\n"
msgstr ""
"他们把奇科关在哪？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 5530..6645
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/6
msgid ""
"One of the houses, most likely. You can peek\n"
"through the doors.\n"
msgstr ""
"很可能在某间房里。可从\n"
"门缝偷看。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 6659..7523
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/7
msgid ""
"Just press <I=ACT> when the Icon appears.\n"
msgstr ""
"图标出现时按<I=ACT>。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 7718..8735
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/8
msgid ""
"You could also listen to any sounds inside for clues.\n"
msgstr ""
"也可以听听里面的声音找线索。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 8749..9013
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/9
msgid ""
"Good idea.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 9041..10198
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/10
msgid ""
"Guards will still be on the move while you're looking\n"
"inside. Make sure you don't get caught.\n"
msgstr ""
"你查看里面时，守卫仍在移动。\n"
"确保不要被抓到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 10212..10407
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/11
msgid ""
"And Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 10421..11187
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/12
msgid ""
"I know. I'll bring him back.\n"
msgstr ""
"知道，我带他回来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 11201..12051
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/13
msgid ""
"Thank you. I know I can count on you.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢。我就知道能靠你。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, do you know the way to the rail terminal?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，去铁路终端怎么走？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/1
msgid ""
"Remember the locomotive? By the fork in the road\n"
"before the village?\n"
msgstr ""
"还记得那辆机车吗？就在村庄前\n"
"的那个岔路口？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, back in the jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，丛林里那台。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/3
msgid ""
"Follow the train tracks from there and you'll come\n"
"to the terminal.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那里沿着铁轨走，你就会到达\n"
"终点站。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/4
msgid ""
"But there's a plant along the way.\n"
msgstr ""
"但路上有个工厂。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/5
msgid ""
"Disguised as a coffee factory?\n"
msgstr ""
"伪装成咖啡厂那个？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/6
msgid ""
"...Yes, it is their drug refining plant. La CIA controls\n"
"it now.\n"
msgstr ""
"……是的，那是他们的毒品提炼厂。现在由中情局控制\n"
"着。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/7
msgid ""
"Cutting through there is the shortest way, but it'll\n"
"be crawling with soldiers.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那里穿过去是最短的路，但那里\n"
"会布满士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/8
msgid ""
"If you want go around...\n"
msgstr ""
"想绕路的话……\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/9
msgid ""
"No, forget it. If that's the shortest way, that's the\n"
"way I'll take.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，算了。如果那是最短的路，那我就走那\n"
"条路。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/10
msgid ""
"Besides, it's one of their bases. It'll be good intel.\n"
msgstr ""
"何况那是他们的基地，能搞到情报。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/11
msgid ""
"Very good. A number of the guards at the plant\n"
"are positioned on high walkways.\n"
msgstr ""
"很好。工厂里的一些守卫\n"
"驻守在高处的走道上。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/12
msgid ""
"Be sure to study their movements before you\n"
"advance.\n"
msgstr ""
"前进前一定要摸清他们的\n"
"行动规律。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/13
msgid ""
"Or I could just snipe them first...\n"
msgstr ""
"或者先狙掉他们……\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/14
msgid ""
"The plant's layout is another maze, I'm afraid. Stay\n"
"cool.\n"
msgstr ""
"恐怕工厂布局又是个迷宫。保持\n"
"冷静。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/15
msgid ""
"Make your way out of the plant and you'll arrive at\n"
"the terminal.\n"
msgstr ""
"从工厂里出去，你就会到达\n"
"终点站。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/16
msgid ""
"You know a lot about this place...\n"
msgstr ""
"你对这地方很熟……\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/17
msgid ""
"What are you saying? I've been there before -\n"
"when the KGB ran it - yes,\n"
msgstr ""
"你说啥？我以前去过那，\n"
"当时克格勃管的，是的，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/18
msgid ""
"but it is not as if I enjoyed it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我可没觉得享受。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/19
msgid ""
"No, I just meant you know a lot about how the\n"
"enemy works.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我只是说你很了解\n"
"敌人的运作方式。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/20
msgid ""
"I hope so.\n"
msgstr ""
"但愿如此。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/21
msgid ""
"Anyway, did you talk to Chico about the terminal?\n"
msgstr ""
"对了，你跟奇科聊过终端吗？\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/22
msgid ""
"He said it's where they transfer the cargo onto\n"
"trucks.\n"
msgstr ""
"他说那是把货物转到\n"
"卡车上的地方。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/23
msgid ""
"Meaning the facility is of considerable importance\n"
"to them. Don't get careless.\n"
msgstr ""
"这意味着该设施对他们来说相当重要。\n"
"别大意。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/24
msgid ""
"I won't.\n"
msgstr ""
"不会的。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/25
msgid ""
"By the way,\n"
msgstr ""
"对了，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/26
msgid ""
"I've heard of a shortcut that cuts straight to the\n"
"coffee factory to the east of the village,\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说有条近路能直接通到村子东边的\n"
"咖啡工厂，\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/27
msgid ""
"but I've never used it myself. Check it out if you're\n"
"interested.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过我自己没走过。有兴趣的话\n"
"去看看吧。\n"

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/28
msgid ""
"Thanks for the tip.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1226
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/0
msgid ""
"An enemy tank! Is there somewhere you can hide,\n"
"Boss?\n"
msgstr ""
"敌方坦克！Boss，有地方躲\n"
"吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 1253..2215
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/1
msgid ""
"There are train cars, but they won't hold up\n"
"against a gun like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"有火车车厢，但它们挡不住\n"
"那样的炮火。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 2243..2869
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/2
msgid ""
"Even a freight train? Incredible!\n"
msgstr ""
"连货运列车都挡不住？厉害！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 3009..3887
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/3
msgid ""
"But they'd keep me out of sight - temporarily.\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少能暂时让我不被发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 3914..5196
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/4
msgid ""
"Use them to look for an opportunity to hit its\n"
"treads or the fuel tank at the back, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"利用它们寻找机会攻击它的\n"
"履带或后方的油箱，但是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 5196..5781
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/5
msgid ""
"Don't forget about that gun, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了那门炮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 5795..6506
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/6
msgid ""
"Or the soldiers. They may try to flank you.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有士兵。他们可能会包抄你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 6645..8219
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/8
msgid ""
"You can also stop it by taking out all the soldiers.\n"
"You can do it, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"消灭所有士兵也能阻止它。\n"
"你能行，Snake！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1657
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, do I have to take the fork in the road\n"
"back to the village?\n"
msgstr ""
"Amanda，我必须走那个岔路口\n"
"回村庄吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 1685..2925
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/1
msgid ""
"People say there is a shortcut. Go back to the\n"
"coffee factory entrance,\n"
msgstr ""
"人们说有一条捷径。回到\n"
"咖啡工厂入口，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 2939..3469
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/2
msgid ""
"then follow the path on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后走右边的路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4082
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/3
msgid ""
"That will take you straight to the village.\n"
msgstr ""
"就能直接到村子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 4109..4820
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/4
msgid ""
"They may have increased security in that area,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过他们可能加强了那片的\n"
"安保。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6534
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/5
msgid ""
"Not surprising, after what happened with the tank.\n"
"What do I do once I'm back at the village?\n"
msgstr ""
"在坦克那件事之后，这并不奇怪。\n"
"回到村庄后我该做什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 6561..8010
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/6
msgid ""
"Destroy the barricade at the north side. From\n"
"there you can reconnect with the transport route.\n"
msgstr ""
"摧毁北侧的路障。从\n"
"那里你可以重新接上运输路线。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 8024..8874
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/7
msgid ""
"Hmm... I'll need C4 for that.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……那需要C4。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9738
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/8
msgid ""
"The explosion will bring everyone running too.\n"
msgstr ""
"爆炸也会把所有人引过来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10727
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/9
msgid ""
"There's probably going to be a fight - one way or\n"
"the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"很可能会有一场战斗——不管\n"
"怎样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 10755..11730
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/10
msgid ""
"They might not see you if you stick to the\n"
"narrower pathways.\n"
msgstr ""
"走\n"
"窄路，他们可能看不到你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 11800..12552
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/11
msgid ""
"Then just climb over any obstacles.\n"
msgstr ""
"遇到障碍直接翻过去。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 12566..13583
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/12
msgid ""
"Don't let your guard down after taking out the\n"
"barricade, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"摧毁路障后也不要\n"
"放松警惕。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 445..1226
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/0
msgid ""
"Chico says there's a bridge north of the village.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科说村北有座桥。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 1253..2020
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/1
msgid ""
"Yes, a narrow one - for crossing the pipe.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，很窄，只能过管道。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 2159..2981
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/2
msgid ""
"On the other side of that is the road the trucks\n"
"use,\n"
msgstr ""
"在另一侧是卡车\n"
"使用的道路，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 3023..3482
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/3
msgid ""
"though it's collapsed in places.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过有些地方塌了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 3622..4249
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/4
msgid ""
"I'll have nowhere to run if they spot me.\n"
msgstr ""
"被他们发现我就没处跑了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 4263..4792
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/5
msgid ""
"They could be blocking the road, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们可能也封了路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 4820..5182
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/6
msgid ""
"Is there another way?\n"
msgstr ""
"还有别的路？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 5196..5851
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/7
msgid ""
"There is a path along the cliff.\n"
msgstr ""
"悬崖边有条小路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6993
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/8
msgid ""
"After you cross the bridge, there are ruins of a\n"
"fort on the mountain.\n"
msgstr ""
"过桥后，山上有一座\n"
"堡垒废墟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 7049..7704
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/9
msgid ""
"Going through there would be a little easier.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那儿走会容易些。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 7746..8888
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/10
msgid ""
"Once you come to the end of the mountain path,\n"
"you'll be at the fort.\n"
msgstr ""
"山路走到头，\n"
"就到堡垒了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 431..1950
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/0
msgid ""
"That fort was built during the civil war. It seems la\n"
"CIA's troops are occupying it, now.\n"
msgstr ""
"那堡垒是内战时期建的。现在\n"
"似乎被CIA的部队占了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 2187..2856
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/1
msgid ""
"This just gets better and better.\n"
msgstr ""
"真是越来越妙了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 2883..3859
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/2
msgid ""
"They've got gun turrets set up all around, from the\n"
"looks of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"看样子，周围\n"
"架满了炮塔。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 3887..4959
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/3
msgid ""
"Attract too much attention and you'll really stir up\n"
"the hornet's nest.\n"
msgstr ""
"太引人注意的话，\n"
"你会捅了马蜂窝。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 4973..5558
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/4
msgid ""
"Maybe I'll try and find a way around.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许我该另找条路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 5600..6854
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/5
msgid ""
"You could always commandeer one of the turrets -\n"
"a little target practice, perhaps?\n"
msgstr ""
"你随时可以夺下一座炮塔——\n"
"顺便练练枪？\n"

#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/6
msgid ""
"Just like Krasnogorje.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像克拉斯诺戈里那样。\n"

#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/7
msgid ""
"Krasno-what?\n"
msgstr ""
"克拉斯诺什么？\n"

#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/8
msgid ""
"Sorry, just... thinking about old times.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉，只是……想起了往事。\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/0
msgid ""
"Watch out! It's el galápago!\n"
msgstr ""
"当心！是el galápago！\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/1
msgid ""
"It reduces its body weight by blasting air\n"
"underneath it.\n"
msgstr ""
"它靠往下喷气\n"
"减轻体重。\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/2
msgid ""
"That makes it a lot faster than any tank. It also\n"
"has a tight turning radius.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以比坦克快得多，\n"
"转向也灵活。\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/3
msgid ""
"Any weak points?\n"
msgstr ""
"弱点在哪？\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/4
msgid ""
"Taking out its boosters could reduce its\n"
"acceleration...\n"
msgstr ""
"打掉助推器可以降低\n"
"它的加速……\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/5
msgid ""
"You could also try destroying its machine guns.\n"
msgstr ""
"也可以试试打掉它的机枪。\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/6
msgid ""
"I'll give it a shot.\n"
msgstr ""
"我试试看。\n"

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/7
msgid ""
"We've lost many compas to that thing. Send it to\n"
"the scrapyard!\n"
msgstr ""
"它害我们损失不少弟兄。送它去\n"
"废铁场！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 459..1894
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/0
msgid ""
"From here on in you'll be in a cloud forest. The\n"
"ground is covered in vegetation.\n"
msgstr ""
"从这里开始就是云雾林了。地面\n"
"被植被覆盖。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2897
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/1
msgid ""
"You'll have plenty of hiding places, but so will the\n"
"enemy.\n"
msgstr ""
"你有不少藏身之处，但敌人\n"
"也一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 2925..3496
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/2
msgid ""
"I'll keep an eye out for scouts.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会留意侦察兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 3524..4360
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/3
msgid ""
"Trying to force your way through would be suicide.\n"
msgstr ""
"硬闯等于送死。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 4388..5377
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/4
msgid ""
"Know the enemy's location before making any\n"
"moves.\n"
msgstr ""
"行动前先摸清敌人\n"
"位置。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 5405..6004
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/5
msgid ""
"Too bad you don't have some sort of radar.\n"
msgstr ""
"可惜你没有雷达之类的东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 6227..6715
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/6
msgid ""
"I could try night vision.\n"
msgstr ""
"我可以试试夜视。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 6729..7843
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/7
msgid ""
"Once you know where an enemy is, decide how you\n"
"want to handle him.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦知道敌人的位置，就决定怎么\n"
"对付他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 7871..8373
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/8
msgid ""
"You could get into his blindspots...\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以绕进他的盲区……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 8414..9626
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/9
msgid ""
"Or drop him from a distance before he even has a\n"
"clue someone's around.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者在他还没察觉有人靠近时\n"
"就远距离放倒他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 9640..10267
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/10
msgid ""
"An eye for an eye, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"以眼还眼，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 431..1323
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/0
msgid ""
"Don't even think about facing a chopper head-on.\n"
msgstr ""
"想都别想正面硬刚直升机。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2145
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/1
msgid ""
"Guerilla tactics would work well in a place like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"那种地形打游击最合适。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 2159..3357
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/2
msgid ""
"Moving from tree to tree will make it hard to get a\n"
"fix on you from the air.\n"
msgstr ""
"在树与树之间移动，空中就很难\n"
"锁定你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 3385..3747
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/3
msgid ""
"That's your best chance.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是你最好的机会。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 3761..4862
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/4
msgid ""
"Good thinking, comandante. You clearly know your\n"
"way around a battlefield.\n"
msgstr ""
"好主意，指挥官。你显然熟悉\n"
"战场。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 4876..6060
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/5
msgid ""
"Enough, Boss. Time to stop talking and start using\n"
"your ears.\n"
msgstr ""
"够了，Boss。别说了，用\n"
"耳朵听。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 6074..7035
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/6
msgid ""
"When you're hiding, you won't be able to see the\n"
"chopper that well.\n"
msgstr ""
"躲起来时，你看不太清\n"
"直升机。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 7063..8052
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/7
msgid ""
"It's important to use sound to get a read on its\n"
"position.\n"
msgstr ""
"靠声音判断它的位置\n"
"很重要。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9543
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/8
msgid ""
"You could also try taking out its tail rotor. That\n"
"would greatly reduce its mobility.\n"
msgstr ""
"也可以试试打掉它的尾桨。那会\n"
"大大降低它的机动性。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 9571..10044
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/9
msgid ""
"And watch out for ground troops.\n"
msgstr ""
"还要小心地面部队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 10058..10630
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/10
msgid ""
"Copy that, comandante.\n"
msgstr ""
"收到，指挥官。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 445..1226
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/0
msgid ""
"The paths there are buried in vegetation.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里植被茂密，路都被埋了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 1239..2410
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/1
msgid ""
"Work with nature to conceal yourself, and you'll be\n"
"much harder to spot.\n"
msgstr ""
"利用自然环境隐蔽自己，\n"
"就很难被发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 2563..3204
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/2
msgid ""
"A ghillie suit would be perfect here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里穿吉利服最合适。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 3232..4667
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/3
msgid ""
"In any case, take caution when advancing. Don't\n"
"wear anything that stands out.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，前进时要小心。别穿\n"
"显眼的衣服。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 4681..5642
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/4
msgid ""
"The ruins are a labyrinth, so try and keep your\n"
"bearings.\n"
msgstr ""
"遗迹像迷宫一样，注意\n"
"别迷失方向。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6408
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/5
msgid ""
"I can use those walls to stay out of sight.\n"
msgstr ""
"我可以借那些墙来藏身。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 6436..7481
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/6
msgid ""
"Once a sniper is spotted, he'll move to another\n"
"location.\n"
msgstr ""
"狙击手一旦暴露，就会转移到\n"
"别的位置。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 7495..8178
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/7
msgid ""
"You shouldn't stick to the same place, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"你也不能老待在一个地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 8317..9348
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/8
msgid ""
"I know. I learned all about that in the Soviet Union.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。我在苏联都学过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 9376..10825
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/9
msgid ""
"It's not necessarily a good idea to try to engage a\n"
"sniper in close-quarters combat.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟狙击手打近身战\n"
"未必是好主意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 10853..12134
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/10
msgid ""
"Finally, once you've found a place to hide don't let\n"
"them take you from behind.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后，找到藏身处后别让\n"
"他们从背后偷袭你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0100_000_0
#. timeline 12176..13277
#: codec/1/204/0xccb20/11
msgid ""
"Don't worry. No one sneaks up on me.\n"
msgstr ""
"放心。没人能靠近我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 445..1504
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/0
msgid ""
"El colibri may be powerful, but he can be defeated.\n"
msgstr ""
"蜂鸟虽强，但并非不可战胜。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 1532..2326
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/1
msgid ""
"Looks like you have a lot of places to hide there.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来那里能藏身的地方很多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 2354..3650
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/2
msgid ""
"Remember your fight with the other chopper.\n"
"Guerilla tactics will be key.\n"
msgstr ""
"回想你跟另一架直升机的战斗。\n"
"游击战术是关键。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 3678..4555
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/3
msgid ""
"Only this one's got a few more aces up its sleeve.\n"
msgstr ""
"只不过这架还藏着几张王牌。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 4569..5586
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/4
msgid ""
"Yes. It might try to crush you by taking out the\n"
"pillars.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。它可能会打掉柱子\n"
"来压你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 5614..7077
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/5
msgid ""
"Also, watch out for the smaller craft that abducted\n"
"Chico, the chicolibrí.\n"
msgstr ""
"还要小心抓走奇科的那架小飞机，\n"
"奇科蜂鸟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 7105..7509
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/6
msgid ""
"Chicolibrí...\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科蜂鸟\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 7537..9055
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/7
msgid ""
"It means \"son of colibri.\" If it gets you, you'll just\n"
"have to wriggle your way out.\n"
msgstr ""
"意思是“蜂鸟之子”。要是被抓住，\n"
"你只能挣扎着脱身。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 9069..9599
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/8
msgid ""
"You might get away if you're lucky.\n"
msgstr ""
"运气好的话也许能逃掉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 9613..10240
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/9
msgid ""
"I'd rather not have to take that chance.\n"
msgstr ""
"我可不想冒那个险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0120_000_0
#. timeline 10267..10992
#: codec/1/205/0xcd210/10
msgid ""
"Indeed, that would be best.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实，那样最好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 445..919
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/0
msgid ""
"I remember those barracks.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记得那些营房。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 947..2061
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/1
msgid ""
"They're full of criss-crossing pathways so visibility\n"
"is terrible.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面小路纵横交错，\n"
"视野极差。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 2382..2842
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/2
msgid ""
"Perfect for sneaking.\n"
msgstr ""
"适合潜行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 2869..4207
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/3
msgid ""
"That may be true, but it will also be easy to lose\n"
"your fix on where you are.\n"
msgstr ""
"话虽如此，但也容易迷失\n"
"方位。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 4235..5182
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/4
msgid ""
"You could end up bumping into enemies when\n"
"rounding corners, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"转角处还可能\n"
"撞上敌人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 5948..7314
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/6
msgid ""
"You will get a better view on the roof, but naturally\n"
"you will be more easily spotted,\n"
msgstr ""
"屋顶视野好，但自然\n"
"更容易被发现，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 7328..8289
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/7
msgid ""
"and there are few places to hide. If you're going up\n"
"there,\n"
msgstr ""
"而且藏身处很少。你要上去\n"
"那里，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 8303..9097
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/8
msgid ""
"get a quick lay of the land and then come back\n"
"down.\n"
msgstr ""
"先快速摸清地形再\n"
"下来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 9139..10198
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/9
msgid ""
"The soldiers there do not have access to many\n"
"long-range weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里的士兵没有多少\n"
"远程武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 10226..10755
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/10
msgid ""
"Most likely because of the terrain.\n"
msgstr ""
"多半是地形所致。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 10783..11730
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/11
msgid ""
"A sniper rifle could be really advantageous there.\n"
msgstr ""
"狙击枪在那儿会很有优势。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 11758..12120
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/12
msgid ""
"I'll keep that in mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记住了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 12148..12580
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/13
msgid ""
"Good luck, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"祝你好运，SNAKE。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/0
msgid ""
"Take a look, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"看吧，SNAKE。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/1
msgid ""
"That place is as wide open as a soccer stadium.\n"
msgstr ""
"那地方开阔得像足球场。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/2
msgid ""
"Best to use a long-range weapon you can snipe\n"
"with.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好用能狙击的\n"
"远程武器。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/3
msgid ""
"I can see several exits.\n"
msgstr ""
"我能看到好几个出口。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/4
msgid ""
"Right. Don't get too focused on any one of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。别只盯着一个。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/5
#: codec/2/917/0x395bd0/13
msgid ""
"Copy that.\n"
msgstr ""
"收到。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdac0/6
msgid ""
"Go get 'em, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"上吧，SNAKE！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..1086
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/0
msgid ""
"That is el escarabajo - the beetle.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是el escarabajo——甲虫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 1114..2020
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/1
msgid ""
"Even we don't know the escarabajo's weaknesses.\n"
msgstr ""
"连我们也不知道甲虫的弱点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2633
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/2
msgid ""
"That's not what I wanted to hear.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可不是我想听的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 2661..3636
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/3
msgid ""
"You could try asking that scientist... Huey, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"问问那科学家……休伊，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 3664..5154
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/4
msgid ""
"This is just common sense, but once it fires a\n"
"missile, it must take time to reload.\n"
msgstr ""
"常识而已，它发射导弹后\n"
"装填需要时间。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6060
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/5
msgid ""
"And moving a machine of that size must require\n"
"the release of\n"
msgstr ""
"而且移动那么大的机器肯定需要\n"
"释放\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 6074..6548
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/6
msgid ""
"considerable amounts of heat.\n"
msgstr ""
"大量热量。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0130_000_0
#. timeline 30818..49118
#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/7
msgid ""
"Another option would be to take out its weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"另一个办法是打掉它的武器。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/8
msgid ""
"Sorry I wasn't much help.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉没帮上忙。\n"

#: codec/1/205/0xcdce0/9
msgid ""
"No, you've given me some ideas.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，你给了我思路。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/0
msgid ""
"Wow, you made it all the way to el basilisco's\n"
"hangar.\n"
msgstr ""
"哇，你居然一路到了el basilisco的\n"
"机库。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/1
msgid ""
"None of us has ever gone that far. I have no idea\n"
"what the underground base is like.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们谁都没到过那么深。地下基地\n"
"什么样我完全不知道。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/2
msgid ""
"Wish I could say the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"我倒希望我也是。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/3
msgid ""
"It'll most likely be some kind of building, so...\n"
msgstr ""
"多半是某种建筑，所以……\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/4
msgid ""
"...Plenty of places to hide.\n"
msgstr ""
"……藏身地多的是。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/5
msgid ""
"Right, but security will be extremely tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，但戒备会极其森严。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xce040/6
msgid ""
"Do not forget that the odds are stacked heavily\n"
"against you.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了你面对的胜算极其\n"
"渺茫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..877
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/0
msgid ""
"Any word from Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE有消息？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 905..1699
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/1
msgid ""
"I can't get through. Strangelove must still have him.\n"
msgstr ""
"联系不上。斯特兰奇洛夫还扣着他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 1727..1978
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/2
msgid ""
"No!\n"
msgstr ""
"不！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 2006..2772
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/3
msgid ""
"We just have to trust the Boss - and wait.\n"
msgstr ""
"只能相信BOSS——然后等。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 2800..3134
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/4
msgid ""
"For how long?\n"
msgstr ""
"等多久？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 3162..4151
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/5
msgid ""
"Amanda, you're cute when you're angry, but please,\n"
"calm down.\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达，你生气很可爱，但拜托，\n"
"冷静点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 4179..4806
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/6
msgid ""
"He's prepared for situations like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"他为这种情况做过准备。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 4820..5712
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/7
msgid ""
"With what? They'll find whatever he has on him.\n"
msgstr ""
"靠啥？他身上有啥都会被搜出。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 5726..7007
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/8
msgid ""
"No they won't, because this is something a lot\n"
"more personal than equipment.\n"
msgstr ""
"不会的，因为这东西比装备\n"
"私人得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_amd0170_000_0
#. timeline 7035..7704
#: codec/1/206/0xce300/9
msgid ""
"And Snake would never have gotten rid of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"而SNAKE绝不会丢掉它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 445..1811
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/0
msgid ""
"Be careful, Snake! I have no advice on dealing with\n"
"el basilisco's attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心，SNAKE！对付el basilisco的攻击\n"
"我没什么建议。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2647
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/1
msgid ""
"But you may be able to use its size against it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但也许能利用它的体型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 2674..3524
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/2
msgid ""
"Its movements will probably be just as big,\n"
msgstr ""
"它的动作多半也很大，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4583
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/3
msgid ""
"meaning it should give some kind of warning before\n"
"most of its attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"也就是说大多数攻击前应该会有\n"
"某种预兆。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 4611..4890
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/4
msgid ""
"That's true.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 4917..5865
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/5
msgid ""
"It might be good to start out by studying its\n"
"movements,\n"
msgstr ""
"也许可以先研究它的\n"
"移动方式，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6617
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/6
msgid ""
"watching what it does before each attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"看它每次攻击前的动作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 6645..7202
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/7
msgid ""
"That should help you avoid most of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样能躲开大部分攻击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 7230..8400
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/8
msgid ""
"And weapons that walk always have one\n"
"guaranteed weakness.\n"
msgstr ""
"会走路的武器总是有一个\n"
"必然的弱点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 8428..8735
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/9
msgid ""
"The legs.\n"
msgstr ""
"腿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 8749..9933
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/10
msgid ""
"Right. Destroy its legs and you'll stop it from\n"
"moving.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。摧毁它的腿就能让它\n"
"无法移动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 9961..10797
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/11
msgid ""
"You might even be able to knock it on its back if\n"
"you're lucky.\n"
msgstr ""
"运气好的话，你甚至能把它\n"
"掀翻在地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 10825..11661
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/12
msgid ""
"Just make sure you're out the way first.\n"
msgstr ""
"但先确保自己躲开了。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you have to stop the launch! It's going to\n"
"strike Cuba!\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，你必须阻止发射！它要\n"
"袭击古巴了！\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/1
msgid ""
"I know, I know!\n"
msgstr ""
"知道啦！\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/2
msgid ""
"The situation has changed completely now that it\n"
"has been upgraded.\n"
msgstr ""
"它经过升级后，情况已经\n"
"完全改变了。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/3
msgid ""
"I do not know if your old tactics will work.\n"
msgstr ""
"老战术未必管用。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/4
msgid ""
"But the basic strategy remains the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"但基本策略不变。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/5
msgid ""
"Try to anticipate what it's going to do before it\n"
"does it.\n"
msgstr ""
"试着在它行动之前\n"
"预判它的动作。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/6
msgid ""
"So, you probably won't have as much time to stand\n"
"around staring.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以，你大概不会有那么多时间\n"
"站着干瞪眼了。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/7
msgid ""
"Wasn't counting on it. I'll manage somehow.\n"
msgstr ""
"没指望过。我自己想办法。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xceef0/0
msgid ""
"The enemy has launched an attack now that they\n"
"know where our base is.\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人已经知道了基地位置，\n"
"于是发动了进攻。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xceef0/1
msgid ""
"The time for hiding is over.\n"
msgstr ""
"躲藏的日子结束了。\n"

#: codec/1/206/0xceef0/2
msgid ""
"We have no choice but to fight back.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们别无选择，只能反击。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/0
msgid ""
"Sabotaging enemy bases is another principle of\n"
"guerilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"破坏敌方基地是游击战的\n"
"另一项原则。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/1
msgid ""
"You will need explosives for that,\n"
msgstr ""
"这需要炸药，\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/2
msgid ""
"and naturally once they detonate the enemy will\n"
"know you're there.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且一旦引爆，敌人就会\n"
"知道你在那里。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/3
msgid ""
"So you need to make sure you have enough time\n"
"to get to safety before they go off.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你需要确保有足够的时间\n"
"在它们爆炸前到达安全地点。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/4
msgid ""
"Best to plan your escape route before you go and\n"
"plant the explosives.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好在去安放炸药之前\n"
"就规划好逃生路线。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf5a0/0
msgid ""
"You could always use those.\n"
msgstr ""
"你随时能用那些。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/0
msgid ""
"Sometimes the enemy will respond to guerilla\n"
"activity with numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时敌人会以人数优势来回应\n"
"游击活动。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/1
msgid ""
"Under no circumstances should you engage the\n"
"enemy in this situation.\n"
msgstr ""
"在这种情况下，你绝不能\n"
"与敌人交战。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/2
msgid ""
"Focus on staying calm, carefully studying enemy\n"
"movement, and staying out of sight.\n"
msgstr ""
"专注于保持冷静，仔细观察敌人的\n"
"移动，并避免暴露行踪。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/3
msgid ""
"You must also be careful not to make any noise\n"
"that would attract attention, of course.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，你还得小心别弄出任何\n"
"会引人注意的声响。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/4
msgid ""
"Likewise, it is important to listen for any noises the\n"
"enemy makes to get a fix on their position.\n"
msgstr ""
"同样，留意听敌人发出的\n"
"声响也很重要，好确定他们的位置。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/5
msgid ""
"Do not forget to check for signs of the enemy\n"
"other than sight and sound.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了除了视觉和听觉，\n"
"还要留意敌人的其他迹象。\n"

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/6
msgid ""
"To check for signs of the enemy, do <I=ESEARCH> when\n"
"you're pressed against a wall or prone.\n"
msgstr ""
"要查看敌人的迹象，在贴墙或\n"
"趴下时按<I=ESEARCH>。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..2006
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/0
msgid ""
"The supply staging point is at the eastern foot of\n"
"Irazú. There's a rail terminal there -\n"
msgstr ""
"补给集结在伊拉苏火山的\n"
"东麓。那里有个铁路终点站——\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 2089..3009
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/1
msgid ""
"they'll probably transfer the nuke from the train\n"
"onto a truck.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们很可能会把核弹从火车上\n"
"转移到卡车上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 3037..3928
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/2
msgid ""
"Gotcha. I'll have to catch them while they're moving\n"
"the cargo.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白了。我得趁他们搬运\n"
"货物时抓住他们。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 3956..5057
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/3
msgid ""
"But you might run into el basilisco... Keep your\n"
"eyes peeled, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你可能碰上“蛇怪”…… 保持\n"
"警惕，斯内克。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 5113..6394
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/4
msgid ""
"An 80-foot-tall walking behemoth... The CIA's new\n"
"weapon?\n"
msgstr ""
"一个80英尺高的步行巨兽…… 这就是中情局的\n"
"新武器？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 6520..7453
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/5
msgid ""
"Could be. Too bad it's not actually a dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。可惜它不是真的恐龙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 7718..8749
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/6
msgid ""
"I think they're testing it up at the base on top of\n"
"the mountain.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想他们正在山顶的\n"
"基地里测试它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 8763..9445
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/7
msgid ""
"I met a guy in Russia who described it as\n"
msgstr ""
"我在俄罗斯遇一人，他说它\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 9557..10407
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/8
msgid ""
"\"a metal gear linking infantry and artillery...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“连接步兵与炮兵的合金装备……”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 10421..10741
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/9
msgid ""
"Metal gear...\n"
msgstr ""
"合金装备……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 11201..11828
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/10
msgid ""
"I've got a bad feeling about this.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有种不祥的预感。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 11981..12859
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/11
msgid ""
"Like maybe it's connected to everything that's\n"
"happening here somehow.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许它和这里发生的一切\n"
"都有某种关联。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 12901..13806
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/12
msgid ""
"The nukes? You don't think...\n"
msgstr ""
"核弹？你不会觉得…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 13834..15353
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/13
msgid ""
"...What else could it be? If it is up there, I'll just\n"
"have to improvise.\n"
msgstr ""
"……还能是啥？真在上面，我就只能\n"
"随机应变。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 15422..16202
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/14
msgid ""
"Either way, I won't know until I get there.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管怎样，到了才知道。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 16244..16676
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/15
msgid ""
"Watch your back, Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"小心背后，SNAKE…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 445..1184
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/0
msgid ""
"So there's a real basilisco that lives in the river?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以河里真有活的basilisco？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 1184..2326
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/1
msgid ""
"I'm only saying I heard stories from people who\n"
"said they saw it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是听那些\n"
"自称见过它的人讲过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 2410..3650
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/2
msgid ""
"But I know lots of places to find it in Nicaragua.\n"
"You wanna go have a look?\n"
msgstr ""
"但我知道尼加拉瓜很多地方能找到它。\n"
"想去看看吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 3678..4263
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/3
msgid ""
"I don't have time for sightseeing.\n"
msgstr ""
"我没空观光。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 4611..4987
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/4
msgid ""
"You don't like lizards?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不喜欢蜥蜴？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 5015..5962
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/5
msgid ""
"It's not that. I just think snakes taste better.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是那个。我只是觉得蛇更好吃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 5976..6422
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/6
msgid ""
"...Who said anything about taste?\n"
msgstr ""
"……谁跟你说味道了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 6492..7007
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/7
msgid ""
"How about you? You like 'em?\n"
msgstr ""
"你呢？你喜欢吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 7007..8791
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/8
msgid ""
"Not that way... they do look kinda like dinosaurs,\n"
"though. You don't think that's cool?\n"
msgstr ""
"不是那样……不过它们确实有点像恐龙。\n"
"你不觉得很酷？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 8944..10170
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/9
msgid ""
"They're both reptiles, yeah. But there's a big\n"
"difference size-wise.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们都是爬行动物，没错。但体型上\n"
"差别可大了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 10170..11006
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/10
msgid ""
"I'll bet there are still big ones around somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"我打赌某处肯定还有大个的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 11089..12385
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/11
msgid ""
"They say mammals multiplied and ate up their\n"
"eggs, but they can't all be gone.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说哺乳动物大量繁殖，把它们的蛋都吃光了，\n"
"但它们不可能全都灭绝了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 12469..13026
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/12
msgid ""
"They've gotta exist somewhere out there.\n"
msgstr ""
"外头某处肯定还有。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 13625..14001
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/13
msgid ""
"Dinosaur eggs, huh...\n"
msgstr ""
"恐龙蛋啊……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 14029..14586
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/14
msgid ""
"And animals are always evolving, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"而且动物一直在进化，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 14698..15757
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/15
msgid ""
"Maybe they evolved so much they don't even look\n"
"like dinosaurs anymore.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许它们进化得太厉害，看起来\n"
"都不像恐龙了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 15770..16592
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/16
msgid ""
"Then you can't really call them dinosaurs, can you?\n"
msgstr ""
"那就不算恐龙了吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 16620..18362
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/17
msgid ""
"I guess not... Yeah, you're right, dinosaurs've gotta\n"
"be big!\n"
msgstr ""
"我想不是吧……对，你说得对，恐龙必须\n"
"得很大！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 431..1630
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/0
msgid ""
"Irazú has more than one crater, 'cause it's erupted\n"
"so many times.\n"
msgstr ""
"伊拉苏火山不止一个火山口，因为它喷发过\n"
"很多次。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 1671..2758
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/1
msgid ""
"I heard most of them filled up with rainwater and\n"
"became lakes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说它们大多积满了雨水，\n"
"变成了湖泊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 27439..44878
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/2
msgid ""
"Calderas, huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"破火山口啊。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/3
msgid ""
"Calderas? Yeah, something like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"破火山口？差不多吧。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/4
msgid ""
"...Hey, I got an idea.\n"
msgstr ""
"……嘿，我有个主意。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/5
msgid ""
"When you get to the lake, can you keep an eye out\n"
"for weird animals for me?\n"
msgstr ""
"你到湖边的时候，能帮我留意一下\n"
"奇怪的动物吗？\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/6
msgid ""
"People all over the world tell stories about giant\n"
"monsters living in lakes.\n"
msgstr ""
"世界各地都流传着巨型\n"
"怪物住在湖里的故事。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/7
msgid ""
"Nessie in Loch Ness, Nahuelito in Argentina,\n"
"Ogopogo in Canada...\n"
msgstr ""
"尼斯湖的尼斯湖水怪、阿根廷的纳韦利托、\n"
"加拿大的奥戈波戈……\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/8
msgid ""
"I can hardly keep track of them all.\n"
msgstr ""
"我都快记不清了。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/9
msgid ""
"They say that all these sightings prove dinosaurs\n"
"do still exist.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们说这些目击都证明恐龙\n"
"确实还存在。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/10
msgid ""
"But crater lakes are isolated. They're not\n"
"connected to rivers.\n"
msgstr ""
"但火山口湖是封闭的。它们不\n"
"与河流相连。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but... you know Mokèlé-mbèmbé? In the\n"
"Congo River? He can walk on land.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但是……你知道莫凯莱-姆贝姆贝吗？在\n"
"刚果河里？它能在陆地上行走。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/12
msgid ""
"So maybe they moved there from some other lake.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许它们是从别的湖迁来的。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/13
msgid ""
"You sure know a lot about UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""
"你对未知生物真了解。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/14
msgid ""
"There used to be a guy in el Frente who was a\n"
"hunter. He taught me lots of things.\n"
msgstr ""
"以前在el Frente有个家伙是\n"
"猎人。他教了我很多东西。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/15
msgid ""
"He even said he once went to a place called Isla\n"
"del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""
"他甚至说曾去过一个叫Isla\n"
"del Monstruo的地方。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/16
msgid ""
"A hunter on Isla del Monstruo...\n"
msgstr ""
"怪物岛上的猎人……\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/17
msgid ""
"Someday, I'm gonna be a hunter and catch some\n"
"rare animals.\n"
msgstr ""
"总有一天，我要成为一名猎人，捕捉一些\n"
"稀有动物。\n"

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/18
msgid ""
"Right after we restore peace to our land, of course.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，等我们恢复和平之后。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 459..1030
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/0
msgid ""
"You ever hear of the Loch Ness Monster?\n"
msgstr ""
"你听说过尼斯湖水怪吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 1044..2187
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/1
msgid ""
"Now that one I know. Pretty much everyone's\n"
"heard of ol' Nessie.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个我知道。几乎所有人都\n"
"听说过老尼斯。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 2215..3859
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/2
msgid ""
"Great, so I don't have to explain. I think she's a\n"
"long-lost dinosaur, don't you?\n"
msgstr ""
"太好了，那我就不用解释了。我觉得她是一只\n"
"失落的恐龙，你不觉得吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 3887..4611
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/3
msgid ""
"Uh, sure, why not.\n"
msgstr ""
"行，可以。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 4625..5503
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/4
msgid ""
"One of the compas gave me a book about it - with\n"
"photos.\n"
msgstr ""
"有个同伴给了我一本书——里面有\n"
"照片。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 5558..6199
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/5
msgid ""
"It looks exactly like the plesiosaur.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟蛇颈龙一模一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 6227..6840
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/6
msgid ""
"...Then why does it only live in Loch Ness?\n"
msgstr ""
"……那它为什么只住在尼斯湖？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 6854..7509
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/7
msgid ""
"Well it probably got cut off from the ocean.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概是被海洋隔断了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 7592..8178
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/8
msgid ""
"Back when Loch Ness was part of the ocean,\n"
msgstr ""
"当年尼斯湖还是海的一部分，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 8219..9111
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/9
msgid ""
"some plesiosaurs became trapped there when the\n"
"climate changed.\n"
msgstr ""
"一些蛇颈龙在气候变化时\n"
"被困在了那里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 9195..10086
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/10
msgid ""
"There weren't any mammals there, so no natural\n"
"predators.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里没有任何哺乳动物，所以没有天然的\n"
"捕食者。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 10156..11048
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/11
msgid ""
"Today's Nessie is descended from those\n"
"plesiosaurs.\n"
msgstr ""
"今天的尼斯就是那些\n"
"蛇颈龙的后代。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 11048..12594
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/12
msgid ""
"Then... wouldn't it make sense for there to be\n"
"monsters in other lakes with similar climates?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么……在其他气候相似的湖泊里有\n"
"怪物，不就说得通了吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 12608..13987
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/13
msgid ""
"Exactly! That's why there's been giant monster\n"
"sightings in a bunch of other places\n"
msgstr ""
"没错！所以其他一些地方\n"
"也有巨型怪物出没的目击\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 14029..14879
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/14
msgid ""
"- like Nahuelito and Ogopogo.\n"
msgstr ""
"——比如纳韦利托和奥戈波戈。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 14949..15575
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/15
msgid ""
"I don't know if there's one in Irazú, too...\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道伊拉苏湖里有没有……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 15617..16620
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/16
msgid ""
"But I know there's definitely something living in\n"
"Lago Cocibolca.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我知道Lago Cocibolca里\n"
"肯定有东西活着。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 445..1365
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/0
msgid ""
"You mentioned the Nahuelito... What is it?\n"
msgstr ""
"你提到纳韦利托……那是什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 1365..3204
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/1
msgid ""
"It's a plesiosaur that lives in Lago Nahuel Huapi in\n"
"Argentina. It's described a little differently,\n"
msgstr ""
"这是阿根廷纳韦尔瓦皮湖里的蛇颈龙。\n"
"描述上有些不同，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 3232..4931
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/2
msgid ""
"but I'm sure it's basically the same creature as\n"
"Nessie. Except for one thing...\n"
msgstr ""
"但我肯定它和尼斯湖水怪基本同类。\n"
"只有一点不同……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 5099..6784
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/4
msgid ""
"Well, according to one theory, it's the result of a\n"
"nuclear test back in the '50s...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，根据一种理论，这是50年代一次\n"
"核试验的结果……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 6826..7969
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/5
msgid ""
"What? There's no record of a nuclear test in\n"
"Argentina in the '50s.\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？50年代阿根廷并没有\n"
"核试验的记录。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 8024..8860
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/6
msgid ""
"At the time the president, General Juan Peron,\n"
msgstr ""
"当时总统胡安·庇隆将军，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 8874..9585
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/7
msgid ""
"was pushing hard to industrialize the country.\n"
msgstr ""
"正大力推动国家工业化。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 9696..10630
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/8
msgid ""
"I wouldn't be surprised if he conducted a\n"
"top-secret nuclear test\n"
msgstr ""
"他若搞过\n"
"绝密核试验，我不意外\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 10685..11187
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/9
msgid ""
"before he was overthrown in a coup.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不会意外。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 11521..12190
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/10
msgid ""
"Sounds a little far-fetched to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得有点牵强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 12204..13555
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/11
msgid ""
"You think? Then maybe Nahuelito really is a\n"
"dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？那纳韦利托可能真是\n"
"恐龙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 13583..14043
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/12
msgid ""
"No, I didn't say...\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我没说…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 14071..14795
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/13
msgid ""
"I mean, it's really pretty obvious...\n"
msgstr ""
"我是说，这很明显……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 14837..15018
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/14
msgid ""
"Wait a...\n"
msgstr ""
"等等……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 15130..15631
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/15
msgid ""
"Thanks for clearing that up, Boss!\n"
msgstr ""
"多谢解释，BOSS！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 15659..16272
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/16
msgid ""
"... dinosaur...\n"
msgstr ""
"…恐龙…\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/0
msgid ""
"What about the Ogopogo? And what kind of name\n"
"is that, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""
"那奥戈波戈呢？\n"
"这名字到底算什么？\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/1
msgid ""
"Ogopogo is a monster that lives in Okanagan Lake\n"
"- in Canada.\n"
msgstr ""
"奥戈波戈是住在加拿大\n"
"奥卡纳根湖里的怪物。\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/2
msgid ""
"I guess it's an Indian name, 'cause it's a legend\n"
"passed down by the Indians.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概是印第安语的名字，\n"
"因为是印第安人流传的传说。\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/3
msgid ""
"A legend, huh. Then it's probably not...\n"
msgstr ""
"传说啊，那大概就不是……\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/4
msgid ""
"There're written records of it, too. The first one\n"
"was in 1872,\n"
msgstr ""
"也有文字记载。\n"
"最早的一次是在1872年，\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/5
msgid ""
"and there's been more sightings since the start of\n"
"the 20th century.\n"
msgstr ""
"进入20世纪后\n"
"目击记录更多了。\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/6
msgid ""
"Uh huh...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯哼……\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/7
msgid ""
"You starting to get into UMAs, too, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你也开始迷上未确认生物了，Snake？\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/8
msgid ""
"Yeah, maybe...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，也许吧……\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/9
msgid ""
"UMA hunting... Now that's a real man's adventure!\n"
msgstr ""
"狩猎未确认生物……这才是男子汉的冒险！\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/10
msgid ""
"What do you say, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得呢，Snake？\n"

#: codec/1/209/0xd1d30/11
msgid ""
"After Nicaragua's at peace again, you wanna go\n"
"exploring together?\n"
msgstr ""
"等尼加拉瓜恢复和平，\n"
"要不要一起去探险？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 445..2048
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/0
msgid ""
"Mokèlé-mbèmbé lives in the Congo River. There's\n"
"nothing mysterious about it, though\n"
msgstr ""
"莫凯莱姆贝贝住在刚果河。不过它\n"
"没什么神秘的\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 2089..3051
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/1
msgid ""
"- it's already been confirmed as a real, living\n"
"dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 已证实是真实活着的\n"
"恐龙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 3120..4402
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/2
msgid ""
"The local people know all about it, and when they\n"
"were shown a drawing of a brontosaurus,\n"
msgstr ""
"当地人都知道这件事，当他们\n"
"看到一张雷龙的图画时，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 4458..5280
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/3
msgid ""
"every one of them said it was Mokèlé-mbèmbé.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们都说那就是莫凯莱姆贝贝。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 5405..6534
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/4
msgid ""
"When peace returns to Nicaragua, I wanna go to\n"
"the Congo myself...\n"
msgstr ""
"当尼加拉瓜恢复和平时，我想亲自去\n"
"刚果……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 6798..7746
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/5
msgid ""
"...The revolutionary movement in the Congo ended\n"
"in failure, you know.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你知道，刚果的革命运动\n"
"以失败告终了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 7760..9348
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know. I wish we could do something to help,\n"
"but Africa's awfully far away.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，我知道。真想帮上忙，\n"
"但非洲太远了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 9376..9585
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/7
msgid ""
"Africa...\n"
msgstr ""
"非洲……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 9626..10421
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/8
msgid ""
"I wonder if El Che ever saw Mokèlé-mbèmbé...?\n"
msgstr ""
"不知切见过莫凯莱姆贝贝没……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 10476..10853
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/9
msgid ""
"I wonder if I will...?\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道我能不能见到……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 11173..12106
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/10
msgid ""
"Best to take care of business here before\n"
"daydreaming about Africa.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好先把这儿的事处理完\n"
"再想去非洲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 12134..12775
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, I guess you're right...\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，你说得对……\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/1
msgid ""
"You know much about cloud forests?\n"
msgstr ""
"你了解云雾林吗？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/2
msgid ""
"Not that much... All I know is\n"
msgstr ""
"不太了解……我只知道\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/3
msgid ""
"there's a world of difference between a rainy rain\n"
"forest and a foggy cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""
"多雨的雨林和雾蒙蒙的云雾林\n"
"差别可大了。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/4
msgid ""
"But they have some things in common...\n"
msgstr ""
"但它们也有共同点……\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/5
msgid ""
"Like for instance you gotta watch out for poison\n"
"dart frogs.\n"
msgstr ""
"比如你得小心毒\n"
"镖蛙。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/6
msgid ""
"Both rain and cloud forests have high humidity,\n"
msgstr ""
"雨林和云雾林湿度都很高，\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/7
msgid ""
"so they're perfect environments for frogs and\n"
"other amphibians.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以它们是青蛙和\n"
"其他两栖动物的完美环境。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/8
msgid ""
"I mean, it's not like just touching a strawberry\n"
"poison dart frog or\n"
msgstr ""
"我是说，又不是说只要碰一下草莓\n"
"箭毒蛙或者\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/9
msgid ""
"a dyeing dart frog is going to kill you.\n"
msgstr ""
"染色毒镖蛙就会要你的命。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/10
msgid ""
"But don't eat 'em, no matter how hungry you get.\n"
msgstr ""
"但别吃它们，再饿也别吃。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/11
msgid ""
"I can get all the rations I need from Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""
"母基地的干粮够我用了。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/12
msgid ""
"No jungle food for me this time.\n"
msgstr ""
"这次不吃丛林野味了。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/13
msgid ""
"Seriously? You're not disappointed you don't get to\n"
"eat wild animals?\n"
msgstr ""
"说真的？你不会因为吃不到\n"
"野生动物而失望吗？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/14
msgid ""
"...What do you think I am?\n"
msgstr ""
"……当我什么？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/15
msgid ""
"Ha ha ha. Just kidding. In Colombia, though, there's\n"
"a frog\n"
msgstr ""
"哈哈哈。开玩笑。不过哥伦比亚有种\n"
"青蛙\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/16
msgid ""
"- the golden dart frog - that's lethal to the touch.\n"
msgstr ""
"——金镖蛙——碰一下就致命。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/17
msgid ""
"How do you know all this?\n"
msgstr ""
"你怎么懂这么多？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/18
msgid ""
"C'mon, don't you think poisonous animals are cool?\n"
msgstr ""
"拜托，你不觉得毒物很酷吗？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/19
msgid ""
"Not if you get poisoned by one.\n"
msgstr ""
"被毒到就不酷了。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/20
msgid ""
"Well, obviously. One more thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"那当然。还有一件事。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/21
msgid ""
"When you get to the forest, be on the lookout for\n"
"Bigfoot.\n"
msgstr ""
"到了森林里，要留意\n"
"大脚怪。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/22
msgid ""
"I... think I'll be OK there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……应该没事。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/0
msgid ""
"Bigfoot is an ape man that lives in the Rocky\n"
"Mountains.\n"
msgstr ""
"大脚怪是栖息在\n"
"落基山脉的猿人。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/1
msgid ""
"In the local Indian language he's known as\n"
"Sasquatch.\n"
msgstr ""
"当地印第安语称它为\n"
"萨斯科奇人。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/2
msgid ""
"And get this: he's over three vara (8 ft)! Can you\n"
"believe that?\n"
msgstr ""
"还有：它超过3瓦拉（8英尺）！\n"
"你敢信吗？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/3
msgid ""
"So he's kind've like a gorilla?\n"
msgstr ""
"那它有点像大猩猩？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/4
msgid ""
"Completely different! Even the biggest gorillas only\n"
"get to about two vara (5.5 ft).\n"
msgstr ""
"完全不同！最大的大猩猩\n"
"也只有约2瓦拉（5.5英尺）。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/5
msgid ""
"And they walk on their knuckles.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且它们用指关节行走。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/6
msgid ""
"Bigfoot's... big. And he walks on two feet like people.\n"
msgstr ""
"大脚怪……很大，还像人一样用两条腿走路。\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/7
msgid ""
"So he's more man than ape?\n"
msgstr ""
"那它更像人而不是猿？\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/8
msgid ""
"Probably. His ancestors must have split off from\n"
"humans at some point,\n"
msgstr ""
"大概吧。它的祖先\n"
"应该很早就与人类分道扬镳，\n"

#: codec/1/210/0xd2d60/9
msgid ""
"like before they started using tools and stuff.\n"
msgstr ""
"早在使用工具之前。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/0
msgid ""
"Gotta admit, I've never heard of Mono Grande.\n"
msgstr ""
"说实话，我没听过大脚怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 1407..2814
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/1
msgid ""
"Yeah, he's not as famous as Bigfoot. He's similar,\n"
"but he lives in Venezuela.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，他没大脚怪那么出名。很像，\n"
"但他住在委内瑞拉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 2856..3622
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/2
msgid ""
"He's not that big - less than two vara (5.5 ft)\n"
msgstr ""
"他没那么大——不到两巴拉（5.5英尺）\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 3678..4374
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/3
msgid ""
"- but he's way more ferocious than Bigfoot.\n"
msgstr ""
"——但比大脚怪凶残多了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 4820..6199
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/4
msgid ""
"I wonder just how mean he is? Like when he\n"
"catches his prey, does he punch it to death...?\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道他到底多凶？比如抓到猎物时，\n"
"会不会把它揍死……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 6213..7941
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/5
msgid ""
"That's the law of the wild: you catch your prey,\n"
"you kill it, and you eat it.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是丛林法则：抓住猎物，\n"
"杀死它，然后吃掉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 7955..8888
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/6
msgid ""
"Yeah! Yeah! But punching is way more ferocious\n"
"than biting.\n"
msgstr ""
"对！对！但拳打可比嘴咬凶狠多了\n"
"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 9083..10017
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/7
msgid ""
"Maybe it seems that way because that's what\n"
"humans do.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许因为人类这么干，\n"
"才显得凶残。\n"
